<title>HONG KONG: Seaunion 1996 net loss HK$8.13 mln.</title>
<headline>Seaunion 1996 net loss HK$8.13 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (U.S. cents)	   0.27 loss vs 0.036 gain</p>
<p>    Dividend (U.S. cents)    nil	 vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  8.44 loss vs 1.72 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    8.13 loss vs 0.93 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover		     16.98     vs 13.27</p>
<p>    Company name		 Seaunion Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Seaunion is an oil exploration and development company.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss of HK$6.97 million on loan to Maxvale Investment Ltd, loss of HK$0.39 million on advances to former appointed advisers, loss of HK$0.10 million on write-down of cost of fixed assets, loss of HK$1.2 million on redemption of convertible redeemable note and gain of HK$0.23 million from income in respect of capitalised petroleum expenditure.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs nil.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
